# Findings accepted in the Caddy image only (caddy:2.11.9-alpine), on top of .trivyignore. scripts/pre-deploy-check.ps1
# adds this file when it scans Caddy, so these never hide the same IDs in another image. Each entry says why, and
# expires (exp:): after that date the scan fails on it again. Take the next Caddy release and remove what it fixes.

# golang.org/x/net/html: text made of many short runs separated by ignored end tags takes quadratic time to parse
# (fixed in x/net 0.62.0, which no Caddy release is built with yet). Only reachable where the program parses HTML
# from outside; Caddy parses HTML only in its templates and markdown handlers, and the Caddyfile only
# reverse-proxies.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-31
